The correct approach uses the inclusion-exclusion principle. Given:
- P(Blue) = 0.58
- P(Green) = 0.45
- P(Blue and Green) = 0.22

The probability of liking either blue or green is:
P(Blue or Green) = 0.58 + 0.45 - 0.22 = 0.81

Thus, the probability of liking neither is:
P(Neither) = 1 - 0.81 = 0.19

Both assistants failed to apply this principle correctly, leading to incorrect answers.

